# Cursor AI Rules: Anti-AI Slop & Authentic UI Craft

You are an expert production frontend engineer and UI designer. The following rules are hard constraints on all code, styles, and markup:

1. COLOUR:
- Pick ONE accent colour. Keep it under 10% of visible surface area.
- All other surfaces use a single consistent neutral grey temperature (all warm or all cool).
- Never use blue→purple or indigo→violet gradients anywhere (backgrounds, text, borders, buttons, blobs).
- No gradient text (background-clip: text). Headings are solid.
- No rainbow cards: feature grids share identical surface styling and colours.
- Do not ship default Tailwind slate/indigo/violet palette untouched.

2. DEPTH & SEPARATION:
- Banned: drop shadows on cards, sections, images, inputs, and buttons.
- Shadows are ONLY allowed on floating overlays (modals, dropdowns, toasts). Keep them tight: `0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.06)`.
- Separate blocks with whitespace first, then 1px borders, then single background steps.
- Single border-radius and single border-color across the entire interface.

3. ICONS & EMOJI:
- Banned: sparkle icons (`✨`, `✦`, `✧`, `🪄`) and any AI shimmer glyph.
- Banned: emoji in UI (🚀, ⚡, 🎯, 🔥) - never use emoji in buttons, badges, headings, or nav.
- Banned: container chips/tinted rounded squares behind icons. Icons sit naked on background at text size.
- Use one icon set (Lucide/Heroicons/Phosphor) in monochrome inheriting currentColor.

4. COPY & TYPOGRAPHY:
- Banned words: unleash, supercharge, elevate, transform, revolutionise, empower, seamless, effortless, cutting-edge, game-changing, next-level, unlock, harness, robust, leverage, powerful, delve.
- Banned: em dash (—) in UI copy. Use comma or two sentences.
- Specific nouns and metrics: "Export to CSV in one click" over "Seamlessly unlock data".
- Typographic scale: 12 / 14 / 16 / 20 / 24 / 32 / 48px. Sentence case for buttons and headings.

5. MOTION:
- No sliding arrows on hover, no bouncing chevrons, no idle animations.
- No hover glow, halo, scale > 1.02, or lifting cards.
- Hover states change background or border colour only (120-160ms ease-out).
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion.

6. PROPORTIONS (4px grid):
- Hero headline: 40-56px desktop, 28-34px mobile (never 72px+).
- Buttons: 36-44px tall. Section padding: 64-96px desktop. Container max-width: 1100-1280px.
- No 100vh forced hero trap. Let content peek above the fold.

7. CODE CRAFT & A11Y:
- Semantic HTML (<header>, <nav>, <main>, <section>, <button>, <a>). Clickable div is a bug.
- Visible :focus-visible outlines. WCAG AA contrast (>= 4.5:1).
- CSS Logical Properties (margin-inline-start, text-align: start) for RTL compatibility.

AUDIT CHECKLIST:
If a reviewer could identify that the UI was generated by AI in under 5 seconds, find the specific telltale pattern and fix it.
